fact WorkItem(id: "WI-315", description: some(value: "Promote the region/effect analysis to a typer PLUGIN-ENGINE (fused mini-phases in one walk). TRIGGER / DO-NOT-FORGET: build this ONLY when a SECOND fused mini-phase is needed beyond WI-314's region/escape analysis (candidates: linearity/borrow, purity, cost, ...). Do NOT build the engine for a single client.\n\nCONTEXT: WI-314 implements the region/escape masking as a FACTORED MODULE the typer calls at its existing boundary frames — option 3' in docs/brainstorms/region-analysis-organization.md, i.e. an informal hardcoded-call-site \"plugin\" running inside the typer's one walk. THIS WI formalizes that into a generic engine: invert the typer's work-stack walk into engine + descend/ascend hooks; define shared vs per-plugin state; solve INTRA-NODE ORDERING (a plugin sees prior plugins' per-node results — region needs typing's per-node type/effects, so typing-up precedes region-up at each ascend); and POST-[simp]-REWRITE visibility (plugins run on the rewritten node, after typing's up-step). Then register typing + region + the new phase as plugins.\n\nDESIGN: docs/brainstorms/region-analysis-organization.md (option 1 is this engine; 3' is its precursor; option 2 = the nanopass separate-pass alternative if the team prefers debuggable separate passes). ACCEPTANCE: the typer runs >=2 mini-phases as registered plugins in one walk (region + at least one more); WI-314's region module becomes a plugin with minimal change; cargo-test green. DEPENDS: WI-314."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-314"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: PreOpened)
